### brackets around both tr ranges are literal
tr '[a-z]' '[A-Z]' < mixed.txt
>>> SC2021 1:12
>>> SC2021 1:4

### deleting the lowercase posix class is fine
tr -d '[:lower:]' < codes.txt
>>> none

### deleting the uppercase posix class is fine
tr -d '[:upper:]' < codes.txt
>>> none

### set starting with punctuation and containing a class is fine
tr -d '|/_[:upper:]' < paths.txt
>>> none

### repetition syntax with a star is fine
tr abc '[d*]' < letters.txt
>>> none

### equivalence class is fine
tr '[=e=]' e < accents.txt
>>> none
